  {
   "id": "east-deploy",
   "title": "The Eastern Army arrives in fog",
   "time": "Night to dawn, 21 October",
   "narrative": "Tokugawa Ieyasu came along the Nakasendo from Ogaki and drew up to the east of the Western line. Fukushima Masanori faced Ukita Hideie, the Ii and Matsudaira troops and Honda Tadakatsu stood nearer the road, and Todo Takatora, Kyogoku Takatomo and others took the south side opposite Otani. Heavy fog from the earlier rain hid both armies, and the Tokugawa vanguard stumbled into Ishida's men before either side saw the other. Both recoiled, but each now knew exactly where the enemy stood. Ieyasu himself stayed behind his lines.",
