  {
   "id": "ii-opens",
   "title": "Ii Naomasa begins the fight",
   "time": "Morning, c. 08:00 or 10:00",
   "narrative": "The Ii no Akazonae, the 3,600 crimson-armoured men of Ii Naomasa, opened the battle by striking at the Western centre, led forward by a small party of spearmen. Fukushima Masanori followed and engaged Ukita Hideie's troops. Older accounts date the start to about 08:00, while recent Japanese research prefers nearer 10:00. Naomasa had been named supreme field commander, and he was the first to meet the enemy.",
