   "id": "fukushima-ukita",
   "title": "Deadlock in the centre",
   "time": "Morning",
   "narrative": "Fukushima Masanori's regulars pressed into Ukita Hideie's front while gunfire and arrows filled the air. Ota Gyuichi wrote that friend and foe pushed against each other. Ukita outnumbered Fukushima, but he had been forced to fill his ranks with ronin after senior vassals defected to the Tokugawa, so his army was weaker than its numbers. Spanish accounts add that guns from the Dutch ship De Liefde may have been used as field pieces by the Eastern side.",
