   "title": "The Mori hold back",
   "time": "Afternoon",
   "narrative": "On Mount Nangu the Mori troops under Kikkawa Hiroie never came down. Kikkawa pretended to be eating a meal and blocked Mori Hidemoto, who wanted to relieve Mitsunari, and also stopped Chosokabe Morichika from marching. Mori Terumoto himself stayed in Osaka Castle. About two thirds of the Western army never did any real fighting.",
